_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 32
---
order: 32
---
short_label: XI.32
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: Parallelepipedal solids which are of the same height are to one another as their bases.
----
proof:

Let *AB* and *CD* be parallelepipedal solids of the same height.

I say that the parallelepipedal solids *AB* and *CD* are to one another as their bases, that is, that the solid *AB* to the solid *CD* as the base *AE* is to the base *CF*.

Apply *FH* equal to *AE* to *FG.* Complete the parallelepipedal solid *GK* with the same height as that of *CD* on *FH* as base. [!just I.45; I.31]

